columnalign=\"right left\" columnspacing=\"0em\" rowspacing=\"0.8em 0.8em 0.8em 0.3em\"><mtr><mtd><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow><mn>4</mn></mfrac></mstyle><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><menclose notation=\"updiagonalstrike\"><mn>4</mn></menclose><mo>⋅</mo><mrow data-mjx-texclass=\"INNER\"><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"OPEN\">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle=\"true\" scriptlevel=\"0\"><mfrac><mrow><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></mrow><menclose notation=\"updiagonalstrike\"><mn>4</mn></menclose></mfrac></mstyle><mo data-mjx-texclass=\"CLOSE\">)</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>4</mn><mo>⋅</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mn>2</mn><mo>−</mo><mn>3</mn><mi>p</mi></mtd><mtd><mi></mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>p</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>4</mn></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></mjx-assistive-mml></mjx-container></p>\n<p>Then, we apply the addition and multiplication principles. </p>\n<p>Remember, when we divide an inequality by a negative number, we need to flip the inequality sign:</p>\n<p><mjx-container class=\"MathJax CtxtMenu_Attached_0\" jax=\"CHTML\" display=\"true\" tabindex=\"0\" ctxtmenu_counter=\"47\" style=\"font-size: 113.1%; position: relative;\"><mjx-math display=\"true\" class=\"MJX-TEX\" aria-hidden=\"true\" style=\"margin-left: 0px; margin-right: 0px;\"><mjx-mtable style=\"min-width: 11.235